repository-code: "https://github.com/lorendw7/PerfusionUDE.jl"
url: "https://lorendw7.github.io/PerfusionUDE.jl"
abstract: >-
  PerfusionUDE.jl provides a composable, differentiable, GPU-parallel layer for
  physiologically-based pharmacokinetic (PBPK) transport networks in Julia. It
  supports replacing uncertain constitutive terms (metabolic clearance, tissue
  uptake) with structurally-constrained neural closures inside the ODE
  right-hand side, and estimating them jointly with per-individual physiological
  parameters across populations of thousands of virtual or real subjects. It
  additionally provides tooling for parametric and functional identifiability
  analysis, including recoverability phase diagrams and a mechanistic-content
  test that distinguishes a genuine hybrid model from a disguised neural ODE.
keywords:
  - pharmacokinetics
  - PBPK
  - universal differential equations
  - scientific machine learning
  - inverse problems
  - GPU computing
  - identifiability
  - Julia
